# experiment-2 (UniDoc Pareto) output tree — commit the result artifacts + the
# run record; drop the cache and binary resume state.
# The root .gitignore ignores `logs/`, `*.log`, `*.out` globally; the negations
# below re-include the operational logs. Patterns are relative to experiment-2/.
# NOTE: .gitignore has no inline comments — keep every comment on its own line.

# ~1.6 GB regeneratable cache (per-embedder corpus embeddings, parsed corpus,
# exam.json, probe indexes). This is ~all of the tree's weight; everything else
# is small result artifacts.
.shared_cache/

# ── Operational logs: re-include what the root .gitignore would drop ──
# Let git descend into logs/ (overrides the root `logs/` rule):
!logs/
# Re-ignore its contents by default, then keep the specific files below:
logs/*
# scheduler.log + the per-unit stdout logs (setup/finalize/<method>__seed_N):
!logs/*.log
# final status snapshot:
!logs/STATUS.json
# logs/nohup.out stays ignored by the `logs/*` line above (also root `*.out`).

# Per-seed run.log under the method dirs stays ignored by the root `*.log`
# rule (~3 MB verbose framework logs) — the `!logs/*.log` negation above only
# re-includes logs inside logs/, not these, so intentionally nothing here.

# Optuna study internals (motpe / motpe_warm) + RNG/sampler pickles (random /
# motpe) — binary, resume-only, redundant with the readable history.jsonl /
# search_result.json. The run is done; we never resume a study from git.
optuna.db
*.pkl
